    "description": {
      "type": "String",
      "label": "Description",
      "value": "<p>The Geopony, or Nordland Geo Pony, is a small but incredibly strong breed often used to scale cliff faces and delve 'geo's: large, coastal sink-holes. An agile horse, the Geopony is usually dun with a short, white mane. It has a strong, arched neck, sturdy legs that are good for climbing, and very sure feet combined with a compact muscular body. Despite its small size, it can carry or pull a great deal of weight. The breed is usually 12–13 hands in height and has a generally good temperament.</p>"
